==English==
{{wikipedia|Cyrillic}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla|en}} languages, especially using the Cyrillic script, cf. Russian {{l|ru|азбука|tr=ázbuka}} (also Belarusian, Bulgarian, Macedonian, Serbo-Croatian, Ukrainian), from the first {{etyl|cu|en}} letter names [[аз]] (az) and [[буки]] (búki) (cf. Ancient Greek {{l|grc|ἀλφάβητος|tr=alphabētos}} = {{l/grc|álpha}} + {{l|grc|βῆτα|tr=bēta}} or Persian {{l|fa|الف|tr=alef}} + {{l|fa|الف|tr=bâ}}).

